1
00:00:10,377 --> 00:00:14,467
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

2
00:00:16,256 --> 00:00:16,818
[fzzt]

3
00:00:16,818 --> 00:00:18,144
[whimpering]

4
00:00:18,144 --> 00:00:19,459
WHAT THE FUCK?!

5
00:00:19,459 --> 00:00:20,518
WHAT HAPPENED?!

6
00:00:20,518 --> 00:00:22,686
HOW DID YOU TURN INTO THREE PEOPLE?!

7
00:00:22,686 --> 00:00:22,968
WHAT--

8
00:00:22,968 --> 00:00:27,062
SCIENTIST: I hope those people in the
Lambda Lab can get this under control.

9
00:00:27,062 --> 00:00:29,202
GET *WHAT* UNDER CONTROL?! ME?!

10
00:00:29,202 --> 00:00:31,199
I WANT ANSWERS, ASSHOLE!

11
00:00:31,199 --> 00:00:32,825
IS THIS A THOUGHT-EXPERIMENT?!

12
00:00:32,825 --> 00:00:34,949
AM I IN A SIMULATION RIGHT NOW?!

13
00:00:34,949 --> 00:00:37,563
IS THIS DRUG-INDUCED LUCID DREAMING?!

14
00:00:37,563 --> 00:00:41,286
I KNOW I'M NOT DEAD! IT LOOKS
LIKE WITCHCRAFT TO ME!

15
00:00:41,286 --> 00:00:42,999
THIS IS A CABAL!

16
00:00:42,999 --> 00:00:46,261
YOU SUMMONED ME HERE AS
PRACTICE FOR A DEMON, RIGHT?!

17
00:00:46,261 --> 00:00:47,263
SAY SOMETHING!

18
00:00:47,263 --> 00:00:51,528
SCIENTIST: Well, the dimensional breach is
definitely transmitting organic matter.

19
00:00:51,528 --> 00:00:54,535
WHAT THE FUCK?! YOU THINK THIS
IS A SIMPLE EXPERIMENT?!

20
00:00:54,535 --> 00:00:56,367
YOU THINK I'M JUST A TEST SUBJECT?!

21
00:00:57,301 --> 00:01:00,585
WELL, I KILLED YOUR LEADER!
WHAT DO YOU THINK ABOUT THAT?!

22
00:01:00,585 --> 00:01:03,788
YOU'RE DEALING IN FORCES
YOU'RE NOT PREPARED FOR!

23
00:01:03,788 --> 00:01:08,140
WHAT DO YOU THINK A DEMON WOULD'VE
DONE TO YOU?! SHARE HIS LAB NOTES?!

24
00:01:08,140 --> 00:01:09,071
Stupid... well--

25
00:01:09,071 --> 00:01:10,334
DON'T LOOK AT ME!

26
00:01:11,011 --> 00:01:11,901
Okay...

27
00:01:12,790 --> 00:01:14,641
Demon-summoning idiots...

28
00:01:14,641 --> 00:01:19,008
I didn't even mean to shoot that guy,
but they literally forced my hand.

29
00:01:19,008 --> 00:01:22,984
They shouldn't be surprised. You mess
with the Freeman, this is what happens.

30
00:01:22,984 --> 00:01:25,453
Okay, locked, uh...

31
00:01:25,453 --> 00:01:26,946
Well, what's this?

32
00:01:26,946 --> 00:01:29,410
More black magic, no doubt.

33
00:01:29,410 --> 00:01:31,505
Okay, I'm just going to touch this quick.

34
00:01:31,505 --> 00:01:32,294
[fzzt]

35
00:01:32,294 --> 00:01:32,932
WHOA!

36
00:01:32,932 --> 00:01:34,061
SHIT!

37
00:01:34,061 --> 00:01:34,920
NO!

38
00:01:34,920 --> 00:01:38,179
THOSE BASTARDS DID IT AGAIN!
I'M GONNA KILL THEM!

39
00:01:38,179 --> 00:01:40,727
Wait, no! I've been here before!

40
00:01:40,727 --> 00:01:42,230
Yeah, this makes no sense!

41
00:01:42,230 --> 00:01:44,623
I touched this thing--it's harmless!

42
00:01:44,623 --> 00:01:45,854
Right?

43
00:01:45,854 --> 00:01:47,665
Yeah, nothing.

44
00:01:47,665 --> 00:01:49,435
So, what's going on here?

45
00:01:49,435 --> 00:01:51,383
This is the same thing, right?

46
00:01:51,383 --> 00:01:53,015
Or are they different?

47
00:01:53,015 --> 00:01:54,526
Well, here, I already--

48
00:01:54,526 --> 00:01:55,347
[fzzt]

49
00:01:55,347 --> 00:01:57,905
OOOOH! SHIT!

50
00:01:57,905 --> 00:01:59,218
IT'S A TELEPORTER!

51
00:01:59,218 --> 00:02:01,434
WE INVENTED FUCKING TELEPORTERS!

52
00:02:02,285 --> 00:02:07,906
THE NEW AGE OF MAN BEGINS
WITH ME! AND TELEPORTERS!

53
00:02:07,906 --> 00:02:11,809
Oh, my God! I am dizzy from this!

54
00:02:11,809 --> 00:02:14,003
Or maybe that's because I'm spinning.

55
00:02:14,003 --> 00:02:16,994
I've gotta try it again.
Does this work?

56
00:02:16,994 --> 00:02:18,111
It's orange.

57
00:02:18,111 --> 00:02:19,302
[fzzt]

58
00:02:19,302 --> 00:02:21,253
Ohhh-ho-ho-ho!

59
00:02:21,253 --> 00:02:24,205
So, this is what it's like to be a ninja.

60
00:02:24,205 --> 00:02:25,581
Amazing!

61
00:02:25,581 --> 00:02:28,815
Wonder what the power
source is... or why they hover.

62
00:02:28,815 --> 00:02:30,734
Yeah, I have a lot of questions.

63
00:02:31,328 --> 00:02:32,930
Nice!

64
00:02:32,930 --> 00:02:33,801
Dah!

65
00:02:33,801 --> 00:02:37,607
Like, is this Star Trek-style where
it's transmitting my matter as energy

66
00:02:37,607 --> 00:02:39,610
and reconstructing it on the other end?

67
00:02:39,610 --> 00:02:42,118
Or is it just creating
an exact duplicate of me

68
00:02:42,118 --> 00:02:44,878
and I'm really just committing
suicide over and over?

69
00:02:44,878 --> 00:02:45,440
Hmm.

70
00:02:45,440 --> 00:02:46,467
[fzzt]

71
00:02:46,467 --> 00:02:47,043
Hoo...

72
00:02:47,043 --> 00:02:49,095
No, I don't feel dead,

73
00:02:49,095 --> 00:02:52,674
but am I me or am I Gordon #6?

74
00:02:52,674 --> 00:02:54,736
I might not know the difference.

75
00:02:54,736 --> 00:02:57,095
Well, I should continue either way,

76
00:02:57,095 --> 00:03:00,319
even if that means making
sacrifices for the Greater Gordon.

77
00:03:00,319 --> 00:03:01,602
[fzzt]

78
00:03:01,602 --> 00:03:04,534
I mean, I can't think of a cause
I believe in more than that.

79
00:03:05,784 --> 00:03:06,378
Let's go!

80
00:03:06,378 --> 00:03:07,137
[fzzt]

81
00:03:07,137 --> 00:03:07,968
WhoooaaAAAAAAAAAAAAA!

82
00:03:08,644 --> 00:03:10,939
[crying]

83
00:03:10,939 --> 00:03:13,320
My knees hate me...

84
00:03:13,320 --> 00:03:15,906
Why would they put the
exit point there?

85
00:03:15,906 --> 00:03:19,176
Especially when there are
rotating platforms?

86
00:03:19,176 --> 00:03:21,787
WHY ARE THERE ROTATING PLATFORMS?!

87
00:03:21,787 --> 00:03:24,380
IT'S NOT LIKE THEY'RE NEEDED
FOR THE TELEPORTER BALLS!

88
00:03:24,380 --> 00:03:26,006
THEY'RE ALL OVER THE PLACE!

89
00:03:26,006 --> 00:03:28,261
YEAH, WHAT THE FUCK?!
LOOK AT THIS PLACE!

90
00:03:28,261 --> 00:03:32,197
ALL THAT'S MISSING ARE THE BOBBING
HORSE RIDES AND CALLIOPE MUSIC!

91
00:03:32,197 --> 00:03:35,818
THERE'S NO GOD DAMNED REASON FOR
THIS! WE'VE INVENTED TELEPORTERS!

92
00:03:35,818 --> 00:03:38,213
THAT'S "FUCK YOU, PAY ME!" RESEARCH!

93
00:03:38,213 --> 00:03:41,328
WE DON'T NEED TO PAD OUR COSTS
WITH HIGH-TECH CAROUSELS!

94
00:03:41,328 --> 00:03:44,331
Oh, I get it. It's to
double the experiments,

95
00:03:44,331 --> 00:03:48,086
so if the teleportation doesn't make
you vomit then the platforms will.

96
00:03:48,086 --> 00:03:48,371
Fuck.

97
00:03:48,371 --> 00:03:49,539
[fzzt]

98
00:03:49,539 --> 00:03:51,033
No, not that one again!

99
00:03:52,367 --> 00:03:53,464
Don't drop me!

100
00:03:53,464 --> 00:03:54,563
[fzzt]

101
00:03:54,563 --> 00:03:55,067
Good.

102
00:03:55,504 --> 00:03:59,037
Hey, how does the teleporter
know to teleport just me?

103
00:03:59,037 --> 00:04:01,458
I didn't feel any air moving with me.

104
00:04:01,458 --> 00:04:03,167
[Geiger counter ticking]
Maybe it detects--

105
00:04:03,167 --> 00:04:05,514
[Geiger counter ticking]
Oh, joy! More radiation leaks!

106
00:04:05,514 --> 00:04:08,300
[Geiger counter ticking]
This is a great place for a teleporter junction.

107
00:04:09,215 --> 00:04:11,350
[headcrab crunches]
Ah! Fuck!

108
00:04:11,350 --> 00:04:12,941
Where is it?!

109
00:04:12,941 --> 00:04:16,461
Y'know what? You can die down
there slowly by radiation poisoning.

110
00:04:16,461 --> 00:04:19,899
That works just fine for me. I'm
happy to conserve my ammo.

111
00:04:19,899 --> 00:04:20,666
[door buzzes]

112
00:04:20,666 --> 00:04:21,667
Of course...

113
00:04:22,686 --> 00:04:23,570
All right...

114
00:04:23,570 --> 00:04:24,660
Let's do this.

115
00:04:24,660 --> 00:04:25,705
[fzzt]

116
00:04:25,705 --> 00:04:28,636
Oh. All roads lead to Rome, huh?

117
00:04:28,636 --> 00:04:32,867
Seriously, why do we have so
many radioactive waste problems?

118
00:04:32,867 --> 00:04:36,843
Like, we can't find a better place to put it
out here in the middle of the desert?

119
00:04:36,843 --> 00:04:38,103
[fzzt]

120
00:04:38,103 --> 00:04:41,000
Okay, THIS time, let's do it right.

121
00:04:41,950 --> 00:04:42,816
Whoa, shit...

122
00:04:46,024 --> 00:04:47,701
Yeah, that's a great start...

123
00:04:48,587 --> 00:04:53,452
Okay, now here's to hoping it doesn't
teleport me to just a random green ball.

124
00:04:53,452 --> 00:04:54,482
[fzzt]

125
00:04:54,482 --> 00:04:55,706
Okay...

126
00:04:55,706 --> 00:04:58,634
Yeah, this is a great place
to put that pipe, too.

127
00:04:58,634 --> 00:05:01,181
Maybe I'm expected to
lay flat, spread-eagle,

128
00:05:01,181 --> 00:05:03,667
because that makes as much
sense as anything here.

129
00:05:04,285 --> 00:05:06,803
Oh, these are numbered.
I didn't notice.

130
00:05:06,803 --> 00:05:07,752
[fzzt]

131
00:05:07,752 --> 00:05:09,062
Oh, you again!

132
00:05:09,062 --> 00:05:10,667
Okay, time for dance lessons.

133
00:05:11,582 --> 00:05:15,191
Yeah, one-two...
ah, you losers can't dance.

134
00:05:15,191 --> 00:05:17,566
I don't know why I expected otherwise.

135
00:05:17,566 --> 00:05:20,174
Oh, there's an escape route. Excellent.

136
00:05:20,174 --> 00:05:22,319
Is this a bunker full of provisions?

137
00:05:22,319 --> 00:05:25,044
I'll take canned food, dried... anything.

138
00:05:25,044 --> 00:05:27,691
Hey, wait. I've been here before.

139
00:05:27,691 --> 00:05:30,218
This is the other side of that supply room.

140
00:05:30,218 --> 00:05:34,596
Yeah, this is another one of those
rooms with "creative architecture"

141
00:05:34,596 --> 00:05:36,760
that was designed for giant spiderpeople,

142
00:05:36,760 --> 00:05:40,364
because that's the only kind of person
who would find this layout convenient.

143
00:05:40,364 --> 00:05:41,467
SCIENTIST: Fascinating...

144
00:05:42,676 --> 00:05:44,515
SHUT THE FUCK UP!

145
00:05:44,515 --> 00:05:47,485
YOU THINK WE'RE COOL NOW
BECAUSE I HAVEN'T KILLED YOU, YET?!

146
00:05:47,485 --> 00:05:50,194
YOU HAD TELEPORTERS AND WERE
HOLDING OUT ON ME!

147
00:05:50,194 --> 00:05:52,024
I'M NOT GONNA FORGET THAT!

148
00:05:52,024 --> 00:05:53,019
EVER!

149
00:05:53,019 --> 00:05:56,806
Hey, that's an excellent point:
if we already HAD teleporters,

150
00:05:56,806 --> 00:05:59,578
why the hell was my team even
doing the experiment?!

151
00:05:59,578 --> 00:06:03,763
THERE'S NO POINT TO THE EXPERIMENT
IF TELEPORTERS ALREADY EXIST!

152
00:06:03,763 --> 00:06:04,100
BLAAA-

153
00:06:04,100 --> 00:06:04,502
[fzzt]

154
00:06:04,502 --> 00:06:05,370
--AAAGH!

155
00:06:05,370 --> 00:06:07,168
THAT'S LIKE TESTING FOR TESTING
FOR WATER WHEN IT'S R--

156
00:06:07,168 --> 00:06:07,550
[fzzt]

157
00:06:07,550 --> 00:06:08,499
--AINING!

158
00:06:08,499 --> 00:06:11,500
So, what happened? Did they make
this off OUR research

159
00:06:11,500 --> 00:06:14,409
or were we duplicating work for
no reason at all?!

160
00:06:14,409 --> 00:06:16,248
I THOUGHT WE WERE ALL THE SAME COMPANY!

161
00:06:16,248 --> 00:06:17,897
WHY ARE DIVISIONS BACKSTABBING?!

162
00:06:17,897 --> 00:06:18,878
[fzzt]

163
00:06:18,878 --> 00:06:20,377
ARE WE MICROSOFT?!

164
00:06:20,377 --> 00:06:23,254
I'M SORRY, I THOUGHT I
WORKED AT BLACK MESA!

165
00:06:23,254 --> 00:06:23,798
[fzzt]

166
00:06:23,798 --> 00:06:25,290
Whoa-ho-OH!

167
00:06:25,290 --> 00:06:26,987
WAAAAAAAAH! AAAAAAA--

168
00:06:26,987 --> 00:06:27,387
[fzzt]

169
00:06:27,387 --> 00:06:28,256
--AH!

170
00:06:28,256 --> 00:06:29,367
OH, GOD!

171
00:06:30,089 --> 00:06:31,367
Ah, jeez...

172
00:06:31,908 --> 00:06:32,654
Well...

173
00:06:33,348 --> 00:06:37,801
It looks like momentum from
teleportation is not preserved.

174
00:06:37,801 --> 00:06:43,007
That's helpful, but that raises
so many more questions.  Like--

175
00:06:43,007 --> 00:06:44,035
[fzzt]

176
00:06:44,035 --> 00:06:47,172
--wouldn't my heart stop and
resume beating?

177
00:06:47,172 --> 00:06:50,857
Wouldn't each trip be literally
a small heart attack?

178
00:06:50,857 --> 00:06:53,851
I mean, it would still be worth
it, but what's going on here?

179
00:06:53,851 --> 00:06:54,643
[fzzt]

180
00:06:54,643 --> 00:06:56,162
Yeah, I don't feel it.

181
00:06:56,162 --> 00:06:58,300
No, fuck "6"! Not that one.

182
00:06:59,071 --> 00:07:00,367
This is all that's left.

183
00:07:01,061 --> 00:07:02,631
Oh, wait, wait!

184
00:07:02,631 --> 00:07:05,289
What if this is a trap?

185
00:07:05,289 --> 00:07:07,020
Ohhhh...

186
00:07:07,020 --> 00:07:10,486
Yeah, you wanted to drop
my ass dead, didn't you?

187
00:07:10,486 --> 00:07:13,032
Yeah, this is the Black Mesa I know!

188
00:07:13,032 --> 00:07:14,128
[fzzt]

189
00:07:14,128 --> 00:07:17,793
I'M RIGHT! Now I know
why it's all rotating!

190
00:07:17,793 --> 00:07:20,203
It's teleportation Russian Roulette--

191
00:07:20,203 --> 00:07:24,763
an over-engineered way of proving
you're hardcore. Perfect for scientists.

192
00:07:24,763 --> 00:07:26,688
These are chambers in a gun.

193
00:07:26,688 --> 00:07:27,858
[fzzt]

194
00:07:27,858 --> 00:07:31,077
Wow, that's a big one.
Maybe it knows things.

195
00:07:31,077 --> 00:07:32,081
[door buzzes]

196
00:07:32,081 --> 00:07:34,439
No, that would be too easy.

197
00:07:34,439 --> 00:07:36,112
What's going on here?

198
00:07:36,112 --> 00:07:37,251
[electricity arcing]
Daah!

199
00:07:37,251 --> 00:07:37,912
Whoa, what is--

200
00:07:37,912 --> 00:07:38,901
[teleportation sound]
Hey!

201
00:07:40,278 --> 00:07:42,858
OH, PISS OFF! I CAN TELEPORT, TOO!

202
00:07:42,858 --> 00:07:44,167
[teleportation sound]
Now what?

203
00:07:44,920 --> 00:07:46,982
You're not special anymore!

204
00:07:46,982 --> 00:07:48,354
But this is.

205
00:07:48,354 --> 00:07:50,503
This has the answers.

206
00:07:50,503 --> 00:07:51,267
[fzzt]

